<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander von Bach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813–1893</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander von Bach was an Austrian lawyer and statesman who served as minister of the interior from 1849 to 1859. He gave his name to the decade of neo-absolutism that followed the revolutions of 1848, the 'Bach system' of centralised bureaucratic rule, German as the language of administration and police surveillance, which ended after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>'s defeat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1859.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-von-bach.jpg" alt="Alexander von Bach" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Josef Kriehuber · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_von_Bach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
